WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.535
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.669
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.271
And now, we're going to get
to the news.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:09.041
President Biden today attended
the White House Easter egg roll.

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:12.946
However, due to inflation, the
kids all had to share one egg.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.347
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:18.151
"I'm gonna need that back,
guys, too."

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.953
New York mayor Eric Adams
recently tested positive

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:22.121
for the coronavirus,

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:24.791
and it's the first
positive result he's had.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.592
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.595
New Jersey is set this week to
begin allowing the sale

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:32.431
of recreational marijuana,
so now when people drive

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:35.134
into Jersey, instead of,
"What's that smell?"

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.570
They'll be saying,
"Ooh, what's that smell?"

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.772
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:42.642
The Florida Department of
Education announced last week

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:46.111
that the state has rejected over
50 math textbooks

00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:48.681
from next school year's
curriculum due to references

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.482
to critical race theory.

00:00:50.482 --> 00:00:54.420
What kind of word problems
do those books have?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.389
"If Johnny has to buy 30 apples

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.857
for the Black Panther
meetings..."

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.826
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.994
The Boston Marathon
was held today.

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:04.664
It's the only marathon that
starts with someone yelling,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.232
[Boston accent] "Cops are here!"

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:09.135
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.903
[Normally] A Florida man
was arrested recently

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:14.707
after authorities found a baby
alligator, firearms, and drugs

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.543
in his car during a traffic
stop,

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:20.914
so they had to cancel
the gender reveal party.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.883
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.985
Authorities in Spain recently
detained a fishing boat

00:01:26.985 --> 00:01:29.855
that was carrying more than
6,000 pounds of cocaine

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:31.924
in a fuel tank, which was dumb,

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.861
because they could have gotten
way more for the fuel.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.830
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.100
The athletic apparel company
Lululemon will launch a program

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.969
this week where customers can
exchange

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:46.472
their gently-used clothing items
for e-gift cards.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:49.742
Or, if you prefer cash,
there's always Gary.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.779
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.313 --> 00:02:00.987
"Oh, hey, before you go in
the store, I'll pay double.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:05.158
Gently used, super used. Eh."

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:09.528
Gary's not picky
is what I'm saying.

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.530
And finally, a man in Florida
recently broke

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.666
a Guinness World Record by
watching the movie

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.602
"Spider-Man: No Way Home"
292 times,

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.972
and then set another
world record

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.007
by watching "Morbius" twice.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.576
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.245
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

